Z||000008||SloPonti||10-04-1999||09:50 PM||||i put on the lights last night and they have no blue what so ever in them but boy are they bright-i called the factory and asked why they are called cool blue lights and it it because they give off a slight and i mean slight blue tint to them-you can kinda of see the blue on white road signs and the white lines on the road! these lights are cool though-worth the 25.00 bucks because they are super bright and street legal! the brand name is sylvania-i think that is how it is spelled! it is name brand light and autozone carries the regalar bulbs but these are new so check your local autozone in the next couple of weeks and they should be in-at my autozone they only had two and i picked them up! let me know if you guys put them on and also tell me what you think of them!<BR>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000009||Terrybogin||10-04-1999||10:25 PM||||Food for thought- Those of us who have other vehicles that use the seperate low/high beam elements, part # 9005 and 9006, can add some better vision very easily. Just get the high beam bulbs, trim the center alighnment lug and the two small grooves in the socket and put them in your low beam headlights. You will have 65 watt low and high beams and it helps for us old folks that need that extra light and it doesnt cost any extra. ||||reg||14
